WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.750
Lab 2 runs the check on your own exports.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.336
You need a test Entra tenant with
an inbound provisioning job,

3
00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:08.938
and a SailPoint sandbox
with an Entra source.

4
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:10.500
Both reads are GET only.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.232
Export the inbound job's
schema from the tenant,

6
00:00:13.232 --> 00:00:16.875
and the Entra source's provisioning
policies from the sandbox.

7
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.097
Build the alias list, run the check,

8
00:00:19.097 --> 00:00:23.463
and hand each Finding to the data
architect, who decides the writer.

9
00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:27.518
Export mappings only: a schema
with expressions is fine,

10
00:00:27.518 --> 00:00:29.987
but a policy with values may not be.

11
00:00:29.987 --> 00:00:35.119
Back it out in step five: delete the exports
if they hold anything beyond mappings,

12
00:00:35.119 --> 00:00:39.025
and remove the Graph permission
and the SailPoint API client.

13
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:44.540
The authors haven't run Lab 2; follow
Chapter 08's Lab 2 step by step.
